Subject: [PATCH] ppm: reject overflowing header values and short rasters

get_integer() wrapped on overflow, so a width of 2^64 + 1 parsed as 1. And
decode() allocated the whole output buffer (up to 16384 x 16384 x 4 x 2
bytes within the default limits) before reading the raster, so a 20-byte
header such as `P6 16384 16384 255` allocates 768 MiB just to fail with
NotEnoughBytes. That is out of memory on the 512 MiB wasm heap; natively,
libFuzzer with -malloc_limit_mb=512 reports it the same way. Check for
overflow while parsing and the bytes left in the stream before allocating.
The tests added here fail without the fix.

Upstream: none found.

